From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kanaka Raju Nayana <kanaka.raju.nayana@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 12:36:35 +0530
Subject: mei: bus: fix uevent const argument compatibility

When compiling mei bus driver for older kernels, the mei_cl_device_uevent()
function signature is incompatible with newer kernels where
struct bus_type.uevent requires const struct device_driver *.
This causes a compilation error on older kernels.

Add conditional compilation to support both older kernels (6.6-6.10)
with non-const parameter and newer kernels (6.11+) with const parameter.

Signed-off-by: Kanaka Raju Nayana <kanaka.raju.nayana@intel.com>
---
 drivers/misc/mei/bus.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mei/bus.c b/drivers/misc/mei/bus.c
index fcde082..ef82eba 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/mei/bus.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mei/bus.c
@@ -1278,7 +1278,11 @@ ATTRIBUTE_GROUPS(mei_cldev);
  *
  * Return: 0 on success -ENOMEM on when add_uevent_var fails
  */
+#ifdef BPM_MEI_CL_DEVICE_UEVENT_CONST_ARG_NOT_PRESENT
+static int mei_cl_device_uevent(struct device *dev, struct kobj_uevent_env *env)
+#else
 static int mei_cl_device_uevent(const struct device *dev, struct kobj_uevent_env *env)
+#endif
 {
 	const struct mei_cl_device *cldev = to_mei_cl_device(dev);
 	const uuid_le *uuid = mei_me_cl_uuid(cldev->me_cl);
-- 
